 },
 "what_this_is": "The demand-weighted transmission-and-distribution loss multiplier per Charge Restriction Region and cap period: the energy a supplier is settled on, per unit recorded at a domestic meter. Settlement grosses metered volume up by the DNO's Line Loss Factor and the (zonal since BSC P350, 1 Apr 2018) Transmission Loss Multiplier; this is Ofgem's demand-weighted summary of the two for the cap's benchmark customer.",
 "basis": {
  "illustrative_only": "Columns before December 2018 sit under Ofgem's heading 'Historical examples. These are for historical periods, for illustration only.' They are Ofgem's own back-cast and the best published estimate for 2015-2018; a reader states that.",
  "overlaps_trimmed": "Ofgem's columns overlap twice: 'October 2018 - March 2019' with 'December 2018 - March 2019', and 'April 2023 - September 2023' with 'July 2023 - September 2023'. Each overlap is cut so the later column governs from its own start; the overlapping values are identical in both cases.",
  "gb_median": "The median of the 14 regions, computed here, not published by Ofgem. A national reader uses it until the world maps an address to a GSP group.",
  "gcf": "From the November 2025 update Ofgem folds a GB-average two-year GSP Group Correction uplift into these multipliers (docs/market_research/regional_supply_cost_under_one_national_price_2026-10-25.md section 3b). Earlier columns carry LLF and TLM only.",
  "not_covered": "Before April 2015 and after December 2026: no column. Non-domestic metering: not in the cap model (GAP)."
 },
